# Put a number on it

A measurement connects an observation to a number and a unit. A useful record includes what you measured, how you measured it, and what could change the result.

## A simple example

Imagine comparing two strips by bending them with the same load. Keep the strip dimensions and the loading method consistent so the comparison is useful.

**Useful relationship:** mean = sum of values / number of values

## Pause and try

Write a measurement plan. Name the quantity, its unit, and one condition you would keep fixed.

